  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A uniform rod of length&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math> and&nbsp;mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is free to rotate in a vertical plane about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. The rod initially in horizontal position is released. The initial angular acceleration of the rod is (Moment of inertia of rod about <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0014_69efcd8195c2.png\" style=\"width: 320px; height: 97px;\" /></p>"
  },
